  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. The root-cause file is `lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`, which contains:\n\n- `install_collection()` building `collection_tar._ansible_normalized_cache = {m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep): m for m in collection_tar.getmembers()}` \u2014 the custom normalized-name index.\n- `_extract_tar_dir(tar, dirname, b_dest)` \u2014 strips the trailing separator from `dirname` and looks it up via `tar._ansible_normalized_cache[dirname]` instead of `tar.getmember(dirname)`.\n- `_get_tar_file_member(tar, filename)` \u2014 the standard-lookup counterpart used for files, showing the asymmetry between file lookup (via `getmember`) and directory lookup (via the custom cache).\n\nIncluded `test/units/galaxy/test_collection.py` and `test/units/cli/test_galaxy.py` as existing test precedent for tar-member fixtures/patterns, and `concrete_artifact_manager.py` since it also calls `getmember()` on collection tarballs and is part of the same extraction pathway.",
